Second-stage battery read (U-Boot, PM8909 VADC `VBAT_SNS`):

```text
gkiw: adc type=8 subtype=9 (pon 1/1)
gkiw: adc ref1250=37495 ref625=31127 vbat=38621
gkiw: battery 4080 mV
```

The PM8909 uses the older VADC register map, not ADC5: peripheral `0x31`,
`VBAT_SNS` channel `0x06`, 1/3 prescaler.  The internal 1.25 V and 0.625 V
reference channels calibrate the absolute scale, as Linux's
`qcom-spmi-vadc` does.  The `pon 1/1` read is the known-good control.

The committed build keeps `gkiw: battery 4080 mV` on the normal path and only
prints the type/reference diagnostics when the read fails.
